/* book exam traps: [Y] = [Z]⁻¹ is a matrix inverse: y₁₁ = z₂₂/Δz, not 1/z₁₁. For the T network 1/z₁₁ = 0.1667 S but y₁₁ = 0.2692 S. | Signs in the table are part of the formula. h₂₁ = −z₂₁/z₂₂ is negative for a passive network; dropping the minus gives a passive network with current gain, which is impossible. | z₂₁ = 0 means no ABCD matrix exists by any route; it is not a reason to try another row of the table. | Δh and ΔT have no unit, Δz is in Ω² and Δy in S². Quote the unit of every converted parameter. | Reciprocity checks the arithmetic only for a passive network. An active device such as the transistor gives ΔT ≠ 1 even when every step is right. */
