/* book exam traps: Cascade multiplies ABCD matrices; it never adds them. Adding [Ta] + [Tb] is the most common wrong answer in this topic. | Do not add Z matrices for a parallel connection. Convert to Y, add, and convert back if Z is asked for. | Check the port condition before adding. Two T networks in series with both common terminals at the bottom give [11.2 9.2; 9.2 12.2] Ω, not the sum [12 8; 8 14] Ω. | Matrix order in a cascade follows the signal: the network nearest the source is on the left. | Parallel connection of networks that share a common terminal is always valid; series connection of such networks needs one of them turned over or an isolating transformer. */
